What this license covers, and what it does not:

- Covered (MIT): the code in this repository (server/, web/, scripts/, test/)
  and the Tournament Organizer name and logo in web/brand/. Fork them, rename
  them, ship them.
- Not covered: the Smash&Clash game itself, its name and logo, its rules, card
  data, characters, artwork and audio. This example only shows them the way
  the Smash&Clash API serves them (images load from www.smashandclash.in); it
  does not license them. Using the Smash&Clash API, the SDK's service and the
  game is governed by the Smash&Clash Terms (https://www.smashandclash.in/terms),
  including the developer section: tournaments with entry fees or prizes may use
  $SMASH only.
- The fonts in web/fonts/ keep their own licenses, included next to them:
  Luckiest Guy (Apache License 2.0), Lilita One and Rubik (SIL Open Font
  License 1.1).
- Dependencies keep their own licenses: @smashandclash/sdk (MIT),
  @solana/web3.js (MIT), @solana/spl-token (Apache-2.0), bs58 (MIT),
  tweetnacl (Unlicense, public domain).

